
======================================================================================================================
  L0  FAITHFULNESS -- the generalised baryon model must CONTAIN the anchor's, and the closed-form priors must reproduce the anchor's quadratures
======================================================================================================================
  [OK] L0a the 3- and 4-parameter density model REDUCES EXACTLY to the anchor's two-parameter one: at f_thin = f_thick = f_M and f_zd = 1 all five components (thin, thick, bulge, HI, H2) agree with mi_aqual_mond_refit_2026.densities() to a worst-case relative 0.0e+00 over R = 0.3-30 kpc and |z| = 0-3 kpc, at three (f_M, f_R) pairs including the published clearing cell (1.90, 0.78). So the extended families provably CONTAIN the baseline and nothing is bought by re-writing the model
  [OK] L0b the CLOSED-FORM priors match the anchor's quadratures to 0.0028 sigma in M_* and 0.0000 sigma in Sigma_* across the extended family (the residual is the anchor's 60 kpc / 20 kpc integration cut-off, not a modelling difference). This is what makes the search affordable: the three STAR-COUNT priors are kernel- and footing-INDEPENDENT and cost no AQUAL solve, so only cells that already respect them are ever solved. Every REPORTED number still uses the anchor's own mass_of()/sigma_of()

