  BOUND SATURATION, reported rather than hidden: at footing(s) ['canon'] the chi2 minimum sits ON the f_zd bound (0.45-3.60, i.e. z_d = 135-1080 pc), so its chi2 is an UPPER bound. It cannot change the verdict: AIC would need the two extra parameters to buy 4.0 of chi2 and BIC 3.2, against the 1.45 actually bought, and the saturating bound is already at a z_d the star counts exclude on the thin side.
  [OK] L6a THE PARAMETERS ARE NOT PAID FOR. On five constraints, going 2 -> 3 -> 4 parameters moves chi2 from 8.58 to 8.55 to 8.45 canonical and 8.85 to 8.46 to 7.40 alt -- at most 1.45 of chi2 for TWO extra parameters, against a 2-per-parameter AIC toll and a 1.61-per-parameter BIC toll. Both criteria therefore PREFER the 2-parameter model at both footings (BIC 11.80 -> 13.38 -> 14.89; AIC 12.58 -> 14.55 -> 16.45). At 4 parameters there is ONE effective degree of freedom left, so *** a minimax 'box clearance' bought with a fourth parameter on five constraints is close to meaningless -- and that is the correct description of the one cell in L5 that clears at Bovy & Rix's 68 ***

